  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Your body has adapted to so many climates that it can regulate itself on a whim. Whenever you meet the requirements to adapt to a new climate, you are always considered adapted to that climate, even if you go to another place. Your body can also regulate itself even if you enter a place without breathable air, or steady access to food and drink, or has constant inclement weather that would prevent someone else from resting, allowing you to survive a week without food, water, air, or sleep.</span></p>"
